# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
"""bakery-ave-fw: the apple-ave encoder driver's run-time files, from this Mac's own copy of macOS 13.5.

The out-of-tree AVE driver (github.com/aquarat/apple-m-series-ave-driver, plus
the Silicon Bakery t6020 port) carries no Apple data. What it needs from
Apple's binaries is made on the owner's machine from the owner's copy and
loaded with request_firmware():

  apple/ave_<variant>.bin              the AVE firmware image (unwrapped Mach-O)
                                       that iBoot preloads for macOS 13.5; the
                                       driver checks it against what is in DRAM
  apple/ave-13.5-dpe-<set>.bin         AVE_DPE register tunables, from
                                       AppleAVE2.kext gs_sAVE_DPE_CfgSet_<set>
  apple/ave-13.5-axi2af-<set>.bin      AVE_AXI2AF register tunables, from
                                       gs_sAVE_AXI2AF_Cfg_<set> (t602x only)
  apple/ave-13.5-<v>-data-pristine.bin optional: the cold DATA the driver
                                       captured in debugfs on Linux, checked
                                       here (--capture) before it is kept

The inputs are the files the Asahi installer copied into the stub's Preboot
volume (the macOS 13.5 "OS firmware" the Linux boot runs on):

  <Preboot>/<VG-UUID>/Restore/BuildManifest.plist       board -> file names
  <Preboot>/<VG-UUID>/Restore/SystemVersion.plist       must say 13.5
  <Preboot>/<VG-UUID>/Restore/Firmware/ave/AppleAVE2FW_<variant>.im4p
  <Preboot>/<VG-UUID>/Restore/kernelcache.release.<x>   (IM4P, LZFSE)
  <Preboot>/<VG-UUID>/Restore/Firmware/all_flash/DeviceTree.<board>.im4p

On macOS the stub's Preboot is not mounted by default:

  diskutil list                         # the ~2.5 GB container with "NixOS"
  diskutil mount readOnly diskNs3       # its "Preboot" volume
  bakery-ave-fw -o ./out                # finds /Volumes/Preboot*/.../Restore
  diskutil unmount diskNs3

An unpacked UniversalMac_13.5_22G74_Restore.ipsw works the same (--restore DIR).

Everything is Python 3 standard library. LZFSE (the kernelcache) is decoded
with macOS's libcompression through ctypes, or the `lzfse` command elsewhere.
The output is deterministic: the same inputs give byte-identical files, and
SHA256SUMS/MANIFEST name inputs by basename and sha256, without timestamps.

Credits: the DPE file format, the Image4/kernelcache/CfgSet decoding and the
pristine-DATA check are ports of tools/ave_fwgen.py from aquarat's driver
(GPL-2.0, commit 9ab14e45281e8f61fb499b760408028171a5f2b5); the AXI2AF file,
the device-row and table cross-checks and the ADT check are new (t6020 port).
"""
